SUMMARY:The Women’s Rights Era: Global and Indian Experiments
DESCRIPTION:Over the past fifty years\, women’s movements have transfor
 med women’s rights worldwide—overturning discriminatory laws\, expan
 ding political representation\, and pressing governments to confront vio
 lence against women. Yet winning reform is only the beginning. Centering
  India within this global arc\, this panel examines both how women’s r
 ights reforms are secured and what happens when they are implemented. Je
 nnifer Piscopo\, drawing on The Women’s Rights Era\, traces how women
 ’s movements\, especially in the Global South\, made landmark reforms 
 possible. Gabrielle Kruks-Wisner examines gender and pol\nhttps://www.pr
 inceton.edu/events/2026/womens-rights-era-global-and-indian-experiments
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/womens-rights-era-global-and-in
 dian-experiments
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
