SUMMARY:How to Reason with Words: Models\, Metaphors\, Metaphysics
DESCRIPTION:f large language models can reason — as they are now widely
  said to do — then the source of that reason must be words. This talk 
 discusses the epistemic order that LLMs are currently spreading througho
 ut our culture\, from policy to science to writing. LLMs tap into a vein
  of rationality in which poetics and rhetoric\, rather than deduction an
 d induction\, play the leading role. They present a new status quo in wh
 at can be called the "accidental mythology" of the modern world. In this
  new myth of reason\, metaphor too easily slides into metaphysics\, unch
 ecked by the model. Leif Weatherby is foundi\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/
 events/2026/how-reason-words-models-metaphors-metaphysics
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/how-reason-words-models-metapho
 rs-metaphysics
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
