LOCATION:Labyrinth Books
DESCRIPTION:The Program in Creative Writing presents a poetry reading by 
 Iraqi American poet and writer Dunya Mikhail\, the 2026-2027 Theodore H.
  Holmes ’51 and Bernice Holmes Visiting Poet at Princeton University\,
  a National Book Award finalist\, and a past Guggenheim Fellow. About Du
 nya Mikhail Poet Dunya Mikhail. Photo courtesy Dunya Mikhail Mikhail is 
 the author of the poetry collections The War Works Hard \, shortlisted f
 or the International Griffin Poetry Prize\; Diary of a Wave Outside the 
 Sea \, which won the Arab American Book Award\; The Iraqi Nights \, winn
 er of the Poetry Magazine Translation Award\; In Her Feminine Sign \, wh
 ich was chosen as one of the ten best poetry books of 2019 by The New Yo
 rk Public Library\; and Tablets: Secrets of the Clay\, a section of whic
 h was adopted by UNESCO as a sticker. Her nonfiction book The Beekeeper 
 was a finalist for the National Book Award\, and her debut nov\nAudience
 : Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/2026-27-holm
 es-poetry-reading-dunya-mikhail
