SUMMARY:Reenactment of the Vietnamese Fisherman V. Ku Klux Klan
DESCRIPTION:The Program in Asian American Studies will be hosting a trial
  reenactment with Judge Denny Chin. Our fellow community will be partici
 pating in this reenactment. The trial will be the Case of ’The Vietnam
 ese Fishermen v. The Ku Klux Klan In the 1970s\, after the fall of Saigo
 n\, thousands of Vietnamese fled their country to seek refuge elsewhere.
  Many emigrated to the United States\, where they found opportunity shri
 mping and fishing in the waters off Louisiana\, Mississippi\, and Texas.
  There\, in the Gulf Coast\, they thrived\, despite long odds and diffic
 ult conditions. Some American shrimpers took \nhttps://www.princeton.edu
 /events/2026/reenactment-vietnamese-fisherman-v-ku-klux-klan
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/reenactment-vietnamese-fisherma
 n-v-ku-klux-klan
