DTEND:20261008T213000Z
SUMMARY:Food Justice Undone: Lessons for Building a Better Movement
DESCRIPTION:New Books in Anthropology Food justice activists have worked 
 to increase access to healthy food in low-income communities of color ac
 ross the United States. Yet despite their best intentions\, they often p
 erpetuate food access inequalities and racial stereotypes. Hanna Garth s
 hows how the movement has been affected by misconceptions and assumption
 s about residents\, as well as by unclear definitions of justice and wha
 t it means to be healthy. Focusing on broad structures and microlevel pr
 ocesses\, Garth reveals how power dynamics shape social justice movement
