SUMMARY:“The Bookshop of Black Queer Diaspora: Aurality against Fascism
 ”
DESCRIPTION:An experimental and conceptual text\, The Bookshop of Black Q
 ueer Diaspora is comprised of a series of fictional visits to a make-a-b
 elieve black queer bookshop and art gallery. The bookshop\, however\, is
  made up of actual artifacts that invoke the real histories of black que
 er art and activism\, their responses to the ongoing legacies of colonia
 lism and slavery as well as their manifestations in neoliberal and fasci
 st formations.\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/bookshop-black-que
 er-diaspora-aurality-against-fascism
