SUMMARY:Applying Machine Learning for Policy Analysis – An Introduction
DESCRIPTION:This beginner-friendly workshop introduces machine learning a
 nd its applications in policy analysis\, with guided hands-on coding in 
 R. No prior background in machine learning is required. Participants wil
 l learn what machine learning is\, the difference between supervised and
  unsupervised learning\, and the types of questions and data for which t
 hese approaches are most useful. Through step-by-step coding with exampl
 e data\, participants will apply several widely used machine learning te
 chniques in R. Basic familiarity with R is recommended.\nhttps://www.pri
 nceton.edu/events/2026/applying-machine-learning-policy-analysis-introdu
 ction
