SUMMARY:Princeton University Orchestra: Ginastera\, Korngold & Dvořák
DESCRIPTION:Princeton University Orchestra begins its season with a progr
 am spanning three distinct musical voices. The concert opens with Ginast
 era's Pampeana No. 3\, a vivid orchestral evocation of the Argentine pam
 pas. Cellist Max Salzinger '29\, winner of this year's concerto competit
 ion\, joins the orchestra as soloist for Korngold's lush\, cinematic Cel
 lo Concerto. The program closes with Dvořák's Symphony No. 8 in G majo
 r\, a work celebrated for its warmth\, lyricism\, and folk-inflected mel
 odies. Conducted by Michael Pratt\, Professor of the Practice\, Director
  of Program in Music Performance\, and Director\nhttps://www.princeton.e
 du/events/2026/princeton-university-orchestra-ginastera-korngold-dvorak
