SUMMARY:Policy Analysis with R: Difference-in-Differences and Event Study
  Methods
DESCRIPTION:This workshop provides practical training in conducting diffe
 rence-in-differences (DiD) analyses using R for policy evaluation. Parti
 cipants will learn to implement both classical two-period DiD models and
  modern event study designs to assess policy effects over time. Using ex
 ample datasets and step-by-step R code\, the session will cover basic Di
 D estimation\, visualization of event study dynamics\, and key diagnosti
 c checks\, including assessment of parallel trends. The workshop is desi
 gned for students and researchers interested in causal inference and pol
 icy evaluation. Basic familiarity with \nhttps://www.princeton.edu/event
 s/2026/policy-analysis-r-difference-differences-and-event-study-methods
